{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (Phase 1 confirmed) — /rebar-debug\n\n**Reproduced** in a fresh worktree off `origin/main` (b9dd6e3) with a non-editable install\n(`python -m pip install '.[dev,reviewbot,ui]'`), mirroring the `sweep (macos, full suite)` leg.\nConfirmed `rebar.__file__` lands in `site-packages/rebar/__init__.py`, so\n`Path(rebar.__file__).resolve().parents[2]` = `<venv>/lib/pythonX` (NOT the checkout), exactly\nas the CI error shows.\n\n### Mechanism 1 — editable-layout coupling (the dominant cause)\nTests that need a **repo-root-only** artifact (files that ship in the checkout but NOT inside\nthe installed `rebar` package: `scripts/`, `hatch_build.py`, `docs/`, `.github/`, `Makefile`,\n`pyproject.toml`, `LICENSE`, `tests/`) derive the repo root from an **installed package's**\n`__file__` via `Path(<pkg>.__file__).resolve().parents[2]` (or `.parent.parent.parent`). That\nis the repo root **only** under an editable install. Under the sweep's non-editable install it\nis the venv `lib` dir, so every such lookup raises `FileNotFoundError` (or, for the real-repo\n`WheelBuilder(str(root))` builds, points at the wrong tree). ~40 other tests already use the\ninstall-agnostic `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[N]` (relative to the **test file**, always\nin the checkout) — these are the outliers.\n\n**Confirmed RED set under non-editable (13 files):** `test_release_guards.py:30` (collection\nerror), `test_build_provenance.py:26`, `test_distribution_licenses.py:11`,\n`test_verify_commit_ticket.py:234`, `test_release_workflow_pins.py:20`,\n`test_check_build_env_locked.py:25`, `test_attestation_signing.py:97/227/354/396`,\n`test_identity_ac7_bff8_heldout.py:127`, `test_tombstone_registry.py:259`,\n`test_engine_dir.py:108/137/178`, `test_plan_review.py:893`, `test_sidecar_enrichment.py:200`,\nand `test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py:256` (a variant — see below).\n(`test_context_hints_single_source.py:30` uses the same construct but reconstructs a\npackage-relative path, so it resolves correctly under both layouts — verified PASS, left as-is.)\n\nThe `test_reconciler_...:256` failure is a related variant: the test computes its *expected*\nroot from `invariants.__file__` (imported from `src/` via the tests' engine shim) but production\n`reconciler_repo_root()` uses `rebar.config.__file__` (installed, in site-packages) — the two\ntrees coincide only under editable. Fix is test-only (assert cwd-independence directly, no\nproduction change).\n\n### Mechanism 2 — stale `hatchling` floor vs PEP 639 (the lower-bound leg)\n`pyproject.toml` declares `license = \"Apache-2.0\"` + `license-files = [...]` (PEP 639), which the\nbuild backend only accepts from **hatchling ≥ 1.27.0** (1.26.x support it but are all yanked;\n1.25/1.18 raise `TypeError: Field project.license-files must be a table`). The `dev` extra floors\n`hatchling>=1.18`, so `--resolution lowest-direct` installs 1.18 and any test that builds the\nreal repo (`WheelBuilder(str(REPO_ROOT))`) fails at the floor. Bisected empirically: 1.18/1.25\nFAIL, 1.26.0/1.27.0 OK; 1.27.0 is the minimum non-yanked version. Fix: floor `hatchling>=1.27`.\n\n### Defect attribution\n- **Primary (Mechanism 1):** `13ad-4c6f-4074-4f43` (commit `7024c357`, \"ci: extend periodic\n  sweep with breadth coverage\") added the non-editable `sweep-macos-full` / `sweep-lower-bounds`\n  legs against a test suite that was never made install-agnostic — the legs have been red on\n  every run since. Recording as `caused_by` + close-class `plan_defect` (the breadth-sweep plan\n  omitted test install-portability). The editable-coupling itself is a pre-existing latent\n  omission across many stories; the sweep commit is the ticket a reviewer could plausibly have\n  caught it in.\n- **Secondary (Mechanism 2):** commit `a001e4071ae8` (\"Add Apache-2.0 license; MCP registry\n  manifest…\") adopted PEP 639 `license`/`license-files` syntax without raising the `hatchling`\n  floor (no `rebar-ticket:` trailer on that commit).\n\n### Fix plan (mechanical / install-agnostic — landable per skill)\n1. New `tests/_repo_root.py` helper resolving the checkout root install-agnostically (marker\n   walk from the helper's own location); repoint all 12 repo-root-artifact tests at it.\n2. `test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py`: assert cwd-independence directly (no layout coupling).\n3. `pyproject.toml`: `hatchling>=1.18` → `hatchling>=1.27` (dev extra; also build-system requires for consistency).\n4. New structural guard test (class-uniqueness) forbidding future repo-root-artifact reaches via an installed package's `__file__`.\n\nRED-first oracle = the guard test + running the 13 files under a non-editable install."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788064410525664236,"uuid":"327a7655-0fde-42db-a897-8dcb321cafae"}